"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[9237],{59237:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"inflyaciya-uskorilas-ohlazhdenie-ekonomiki","locale":"en","title":"Weekly Russian inflation accelerates for a second week as household expectations rise to 14.2%","description":"Weekly inflation has accelerated from 0.02% to 0.12% in three weeks, while household expectations rose to 14.2%. Why this matters for the Bank of Russia\'s October 23 rate decision.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"Russian prices rose by 0.12% over September 22–28, 2026. They rose by 0.06% the previous week and 0.02% two weeks earlier. This is the fastest weekly increase since late July. Sustained weekly growth of 0.12% would produce about 6.4% annually (1.0012 to the power of 52), against the Bank of Russia\'s 4% target. One week proves little, but three successive weeks of acceleration are noticeable."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"Seasonally cheaper autumn vegetables are pulling prices down, but more slowly: potatoes fell by 3.2% in the last week of September, versus 3.4% a week earlier. At the same time, eggs rose by 1.9%, while buckwheat and millet rose by 0.8%. Annual inflation on September 28 was about 6.25%; prices had risen by 4.93% since the start of the year, compared with 4.29% over the same period of 2025."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"In September, the Bank of Russia estimated underlying August inflation, meaning price growth excluding random jumps, at an annualized 5–6%. Summer prices had surged largely because of fuel: seasonally adjusted annualized growth was 11.7% in July and 6.9% in August. The spike passed, but inflation did not reach the 4% target, and the key rate remains high at 14%."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"High rates cool the economy: loans are expensive, households and companies spend less, and prices rise more slowly. But this works better when people believe inflation will slow. In September they expected prices to rise by 14.2% over the following year, up from 13.7% in August, even though actual annual inflation was about 6.25%. Someone expecting 14% inflation sees little real cost in a 14% rate: buying now seems better than saving. These are inflation expectations, and the Bank of Russia warns that high expectations can obstruct disinflation."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"What remains unknown is whether this marks a renewed acceleration or a temporary spike. Rosstat will release official September data on October 9, and the Bank of Russia will decide on rates on October 23. For an ordinary person, deposits still exceed price growth: the average maximum rate at the 10 largest banks was 13.05% in late September, versus inflation of about 6.25%. Borrowing in anticipation of an imminent rate cut is risky, but waiting indefinitely also costs money because prices keep rising."},{"id":"b006","kind":"heading","text":"What is Russian inflation in late September 2026?"},{"id":"b007","kind":"paragraph","text":"Annual inflation on September 28 was about 6.25%, with prices up 4.93% since the start of the year. Prices rose by 0.12% in the final week of September, the fastest weekly increase since late July. Rosstat will publish official monthly data on October 9."},{"id":"b008","kind":"heading","text":"Why did inflation accelerate in September 2026?"},{"id":"b009","kind":"paragraph","text":"Vegetables are seasonally cheaper, but their prices are falling more slowly than a week earlier. Eggs and grains are becoming more expensive: eggs rose by 1.9% in the final week of September. The Bank of Russia estimates underlying annualized inflation at 5–6%, above its 4% target."},{"id":"b010","kind":"heading","text":"What are inflation expectations, and why do they matter for interest rates?"},{"id":"b011","kind":"paragraph","text":"They are the price growth people expect over the following year: 14.2% in September 2026. If someone expects that increase, a 14% interest rate has little real cost and they do not postpone purchases. High expectations therefore make it harder for the Bank of Russia to cut rates."}],"sources":[{"label":"Weekly inflation reaches 0.12%","url":"https://www.vedomosti.ru/economics/news/2026/09/30/1233212-nedelnaya-inflyatsiya"},{"label":"Weekly inflation in Russia accelerates to 0.06%","url":"https://www.vedomosti.ru/economics/news/2026/09/23/1231274-inflyatsiya-rossii-uskorilas"},{"label":"Russian inflation is 0.12% on September 22–28 as annual inflation slows to 6.25%","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/business/1119451"},{"label":"Russian household inflation expectations rise to 14.2% in September","url":"https://www.vedomosti.ru/economics/news/2026/09/22/1230887-inflyatsionnie-ozhidaniya"},{"label":"Central bank estimates underlying August inflation at 5–6%","url":"https://ru.themoscowtimes.com/2026/09/16/tsbr-otsenil-ustoychivuyu-inflyatsiyu-v-avguste-v-diapazone-5-6-a206280"},{"label":"Average maximum deposit rate at ten banks rises to 13.05%","url":"https://ria.ru/20261001/bank-2121443529.html"},{"label":"The Bank of Russia kept the key rate at 14%","url":"https://www.cbr.ru/press/keypr/"}],"sourceBodySha256":"a98c31881322940d45b158db2ab6716a039490f89eea6f0ffe309fb1f7594ee1"}')}}]);